1
00:00:00,533 --> 00:00:03,567
It's the first day of the school field trip.

2
00:00:03,567 --> 00:00:04,933
Beelu and his classmates

3
00:00:04,933 --> 00:00:06,133
finish their visit

4
00:00:06,133 --> 00:00:07,833
and return to the hotel

5
00:00:07,833 --> 00:00:11,400
to get some rest.

6
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:13,700
Only Beelu keeps watching videos

7
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:15,600
and has no plans to go to sleep so early.

8
00:00:16,933 --> 00:00:19,100
Aliens really have visited Earth!

9
00:00:20,133 --> 00:00:21,333
On his tablet

10
00:00:21,333 --> 00:00:23,933
is a video about aliens.

11
00:00:23,933 --> 00:00:26,467
It describes how, long, long ago,

12
00:00:26,467 --> 00:00:28,633
aliens helped prehistoric people

13
00:00:28,633 --> 00:00:30,267
establish a village.

14
00:00:30,267 --> 00:00:32,233
What keeps Beelu glued to the screen

15
00:00:32,233 --> 00:00:34,900
and almost up all night is this:

16
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:36,600
the alien village

17
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:37,300
is actually

18
00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:40,700
the place they're visiting on tomorrow's field trip!

19
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:41,933
What's more,

20
00:00:41,933 --> 00:00:45,008
there are many alien fossils

21
00:00:45,008 --> 00:00:47,200
that have not yet been excavated there.

22
00:00:48,175 --> 00:00:50,475
On the second day of the field trip,

23
00:00:50,475 --> 00:00:52,425
the students on the bus are all half-asleep.

24
00:00:52,425 --> 00:00:54,575
Only Beelu is excitedly

25
00:00:54,575 --> 00:00:58,167
looking at the caves in the mountainside outside.

26
00:00:58,167 --> 00:00:59,300
Hee-hee!

27
00:00:59,300 --> 00:01:01,533
I'm going to name the alien I dig up

28
00:01:01,533 --> 00:01:03,833
the Beelu-ian!

29
00:01:05,767 --> 00:01:06,867
Hello, kids!

30
00:01:06,867 --> 00:01:10,225
I'm Bin, a member of the archaeological team here.

31
00:01:10,225 --> 00:01:12,700
Let me show you around

32
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:14,900
this prehistoric cultural site!

33
00:01:14,900 --> 00:01:17,267
The place where aliens used to live!

34
00:01:17,733 --> 00:01:19,200
Do you know, kids?

35
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:25,471
This mountain in front of us used to be underwater!

36
00:01:25,471 --> 00:01:26,653
Bin explains

37
00:01:26,653 --> 00:01:29,252
that the mountain rises just a little each year

38
00:01:29,252 --> 00:01:32,033
until it finally emerges from the sea.

39
00:01:32,033 --> 00:01:36,025
The caves in the mountainside formed

40
00:01:36,025 --> 00:01:39,467
as the mountain rose and the waves eroded it.

41
00:01:39,467 --> 00:01:41,900
So waves can carve out caves!

42
00:01:41,900 --> 00:01:44,167
Some caves are way up high!

43
00:01:44,167 --> 00:01:46,100
How long does that take?

44
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:49,400
The students are amazed

45
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:52,883
by the incredible work of nature.

46
00:01:54,599 --> 00:01:55,666
A flying saucer must have carried

47
00:01:55,666 --> 00:02:00,299
the mountain here from outer space!

48
00:02:00,299 --> 00:02:03,333
But Beelu doesn't seem to be listening to the explanation.

49
00:02:03,333 --> 00:02:06,666
He only has his alien theory in mind.

50
00:02:08,499 --> 00:02:09,833
What is he talking about?

51
00:02:09,833 --> 00:02:13,975
Although Bin is puzzled by Beelu's reaction,

52
00:02:13,975 --> 00:02:18,328
he continues leading the group onward.

53
00:02:18,825 --> 00:02:21,433
Prehistoric people arrived here about 30,000 years ago,

54
00:02:21,433 --> 00:02:23,842
crossing the ocean from far away

55
00:02:23,842 --> 00:02:25,333
to live in these caves!

56
00:02:25,333 --> 00:02:29,267
How could prehistoric people cross the ocean?

57
00:02:29,275 --> 00:02:33,075
How did they make it across?

58
00:02:33,075 --> 00:02:34,550
Thirty thousand years ago...

59
00:02:34,550 --> 00:02:35,442
I wonder if my

60
00:02:35,442 --> 00:02:36,575
great-great-great-great-grandpa

61
00:02:36,575 --> 00:02:38,950
had been born yet?

62
00:02:38,950 --> 00:02:41,614
The story of prehistoric people

63
00:02:41,614 --> 00:02:43,892
makes the students so curious

64
00:02:43,892 --> 00:02:46,381
that they all start asking questions.

65
00:02:46,381 --> 00:02:49,000
Maybe prehistoric people rode flying saucers

66
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:50,633
to get here!

67
00:02:50,633 --> 00:02:51,667
Why is he saying this

68
00:02:51,667 --> 00:02:54,000
kind of baseless thing again?

69
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:54,833
No!

70
00:02:54,833 --> 00:02:56,433
We can't let him keep confusing everyone.

71
00:02:59,133 --> 00:03:00,600
Listen up, everyone!

72
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:02,733
Archaeologists have never

73
00:03:02,733 --> 00:03:04,433
dug up a flying saucer!

74
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:07,833
Bin emphasizes this especially loudly.

75
00:03:07,833 --> 00:03:09,467
The artifacts that have been excavated

76
00:03:09,833 --> 00:03:11,167
and the research done so far

77
00:03:11,167 --> 00:03:12,467
still cannot prove

78
00:03:12,467 --> 00:03:14,967
that prehistoric people

79
00:03:14,967 --> 00:03:16,933
had any contact with aliens.

80
00:03:17,008 --> 00:03:19,433
There's no evidence of that.

81
00:03:19,433 --> 00:03:22,267
Prehistoric artifacts...

82
00:03:26,075 --> 00:03:30,450
Everyone, I'm so excited!

83
00:03:30,450 --> 00:03:31,967
The video even says aliens taught

84
00:03:31,967 --> 00:03:34,004
prehistoric people how to make fire!

85
00:03:34,004 --> 00:03:35,467
Beelu isn't affected by Bin's explanation at all,

86
00:03:35,467 --> 00:03:36,967
because from beginning to end,

87
00:03:36,967 --> 00:03:38,767
he hasn't listened to a word of it.

88
00:03:38,767 --> 00:03:40,400
Beelu is so worked up!

89
00:03:40,400 --> 00:03:41,767
Yeah!

90
00:03:41,767 --> 00:03:43,933
Between aliens and archaeological research,

91
00:03:43,933 --> 00:03:46,333
which one is actually true?

92
00:03:46,333 --> 00:03:48,300
Beelu's excitement

93
00:03:48,300 --> 00:03:50,167
has rubbed off on his classmates

94
00:03:50,167 --> 00:03:53,933
and made them start doubting Bin.

95
00:03:53,933 --> 00:03:55,233
Bin's explanation

96
00:03:55,233 --> 00:03:57,067
has been interrupted so many times

97
00:03:57,067 --> 00:03:59,367
that he finally loses his patience.

98
00:03:59,367 --> 00:04:00,567
Kids!

99
00:04:00,567 --> 00:04:02,133
You say aliens came here.

100
00:04:02,133 --> 00:04:03,567
What proof do you have?

101
00:04:03,567 --> 00:04:04,733
Heh-heh.

102
00:04:04,733 --> 00:04:06,367
The proof is right here!

103
00:04:07,033 --> 00:04:07,967
Huh?

104
00:04:07,967 --> 00:04:09,367
This video

105
00:04:09,367 --> 00:04:10,433
looks

106
00:04:10,433 --> 00:04:11,700
kind of familiar.

107
00:04:12,433 --> 00:04:14,100
Ha-ha!

108
00:04:14,100 --> 00:04:16,267
This video is staged!

109
00:04:17,067 --> 00:04:18,700
No, it isn't!

110
00:04:18,700 --> 00:04:20,633
Aliens are real!

111
00:04:20,633 --> 00:04:23,433
Who filmed this video?

112
00:04:23,433 --> 00:04:24,233
Well...

113
00:04:24,233 --> 00:04:27,700
Some scientific teams...

114
00:04:27,700 --> 00:04:29,167
The students crowd closer

115
00:04:29,167 --> 00:04:31,233
to listen to their conversation.

116
00:04:31,233 --> 00:04:34,533
Beelu feels pressured

117
00:04:34,533 --> 00:04:35,800
because he can't answer Bin's question.

118
00:04:36,733 --> 00:04:37,367
Hmph!

119
00:04:37,367 --> 00:04:39,233
Who filmed it doesn't matter!

120
00:04:39,233 --> 00:04:42,433
I'll find the proof and show you right now!

121
00:04:42,433 --> 00:04:43,500
Young man...

122
00:04:45,533 --> 00:04:47,833
Following the clues in the video, Beelu

123
00:04:47,833 --> 00:04:49,900
comes to a cave.

124
00:04:49,900 --> 00:04:50,967
They say this place

125
00:04:50,967 --> 00:04:52,800
used to be an alien base.

126
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:55,100
If you dig into the rock wall,

127
00:04:55,100 --> 00:04:57,267
you'll find alien fossils!

128
00:04:57,900 --> 00:04:58,867
Hmph!

129
00:04:58,867 --> 00:05:00,567
Once I dig up an alien,

130
00:05:00,567 --> 00:05:04,767
I'll scare you all silly!

131
00:05:07,450 --> 00:05:11,033
Why is this so hard to dig?

132
00:05:13,433 --> 00:05:16,333
Just as Beelu is sweating from all the digging,

133
00:05:23,750 --> 00:05:29,542
suddenly, the earth begins to shake violently.

134
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:38,566
The cave is pitch-black, damp, and cold.

135
00:05:38,566 --> 00:05:41,750
Beelu cries out for help,

136
00:05:41,750 --> 00:05:44,438
but no one answers.

137
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:56,150
Am I going to be trapped in here forever?

138
00:06:04,775 --> 00:06:07,042
Young man!

139
00:06:07,042 --> 00:06:09,417
Bin said that after the tour ended...

140
00:06:09,417 --> 00:06:16,433
I didn't expect Beelu to actually be in here!

141
00:06:16,433 --> 00:06:17,733
I can't believe it...

142
00:06:17,733 --> 00:06:19,766
Beelu really is in here!

143
00:06:19,766 --> 00:06:21,633
Were you the alien?

144
00:06:21,633 --> 00:06:23,200
The video you saw

145
00:06:23,200 --> 00:06:25,967
was part of a puzzle game held here.

146
00:06:26,433 --> 00:06:27,333
The game's story combines

147
00:06:27,333 --> 00:06:29,033
science fiction movies with archaeological research.

148
00:06:30,675 --> 00:06:33,467
It often makes it hard to tell what's real and what isn't.

149
00:06:33,467 --> 00:06:36,133
Wait... does that mean

150
00:06:36,133 --> 00:06:39,767
there really aren't any aliens?

151
00:06:39,767 --> 00:06:40,933
Young man,

152
00:06:40,933 --> 00:06:42,533
even though the video wasn't real,

153
00:06:42,533 --> 00:06:43,467
don't lose heart

154
00:06:43,467 --> 00:06:44,567
so quickly!

155
00:06:45,833 --> 00:06:46,933
Here, take this.

156
00:06:46,933 --> 00:06:47,933
Huh?

157
00:06:47,933 --> 00:06:49,067
It's a stone tool.

158
00:06:49,067 --> 00:06:50,333
Prehistoric people used this

159
00:06:50,333 --> 00:06:51,333
to cut things!

160
00:06:51,333 --> 00:06:52,500
Hmm?

161
00:06:52,500 --> 00:06:53,333
But

162
00:06:53,333 --> 00:06:54,200
this looks

163
00:06:54,200 --> 00:06:56,433
like an ordinary rock.

164
00:06:56,433 --> 00:06:57,733
Ha-ha!

165
00:06:57,733 --> 00:06:58,967
When I first found it,

166
00:06:58,967 --> 00:07:00,300
the people around me said the same thing!

167
00:07:00,900 --> 00:07:02,367
Bin explains

168
00:07:02,367 --> 00:07:04,600
that when he found this stone,

169
00:07:04,600 --> 00:07:05,867
no one believed

170
00:07:05,867 --> 00:07:07,833
it was a tool used by prehistoric people.

171
00:07:07,833 --> 00:07:10,300
Later, he went to the library,

172
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:11,100
searched online,

173
00:07:11,100 --> 00:07:12,433
visited the site,

174
00:07:12,433 --> 00:07:13,933
and gathered lots of information.

175
00:07:13,933 --> 00:07:15,233
He did a great deal of research

176
00:07:15,233 --> 00:07:17,767
and finally proved

177
00:07:17,767 --> 00:07:19,400
what the stone tool was used for.

178
00:07:21,433 --> 00:07:22,767
Although I can't tell you

179
00:07:22,767 --> 00:07:24,167
whether aliens exist or not,

180
00:07:24,767 --> 00:07:26,367
maybe one day

181
00:07:26,367 --> 00:07:28,133
you'll find new evidence

182
00:07:28,133 --> 00:07:29,367
and discover a different answer!

183
00:07:32,367 --> 00:07:33,984
But first...

184
00:07:33,984 --> 00:07:35,984
At the end of the field trip,

185
00:07:35,984 --> 00:07:37,917
although Beelu hasn't found

186
00:07:37,917 --> 00:07:39,951
any alien fossils,

187
00:07:39,951 --> 00:07:42,084
but his curiosity about mysterious phenomena only grows.

188
00:07:42,084 --> 00:07:47,200
Please respect the sign, okay?

189
00:07:51,925 --> 00:07:57,700
He hopes that one day

190
00:07:57,700 --> 00:08:04,500
he'll find the answers to the unknown world!

191
00:08:04,500 --> 00:08:07,875
Today was so much fun!
